<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06L5">Notation <span data-tag="06L5">9.4.8.11</span>.</a> Following the convention of Remark <a data-tag="03PU" href="/tag/03PU">4.9.0.4</a>, an $\infty $-category is essentially small if it is essentially $ \Omega $-small, where $ \Omega $ denotes some fixed strongly inaccessible cardinal. In this case, every accessible $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is essentially $ \Omega ^{+}$-small (Remark <a data-tag="06KK" href="/tag/06KK">9.4.7.14</a>). We let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\operatorname{Acc}}$ denote the subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{\leq  \Omega }$ whose objects are accessible $\infty $-categories and whose morphisms are accessible functors. We will refer to $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\operatorname{Acc}}$ as <em>the $\infty $-category of accessible $\infty $-categories</em>. </p>
